IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `itepa-types`
IMPORT `itepa-rules`

-- Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
-- Seat: the employee.
--
--   "How much is taxed on me for my company car this year, and for my cheap
--    loan? When my job ends, how much of my package is taxed as
--    post-employment notice pay, and how much of the rest above £30,000?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Employee case` HAS
    `the car`                                           IS A MAYBE `Company car`
    `the loan`                                          IS A MAYBE `Cheap loan`
    `the termination`                                   IS A MAYBE `Termination case`

DECLARE `Employee position` HAS
    `appropriate percentage for the car`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `cash equivalent of the car`                        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `cash equivalent of the loan`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `earliest lawful termination date`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `post-employment notice pay`                        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `taxed as earnings under s 402B`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `taxed above the £30,000 threshold`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 120-144, 175-182, 402A-404
@export default The employee's position under the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): the appropriate percentage and cash equivalent of a company car (ss 120-144), the cash equivalent of a cheap loan (ss 175-182), and on termination the earliest lawful termination date, the post-employment notice pay, the part of the termination awards taxed as earnings (ss 402B-402E), and the part taxed above the £30,000 threshold (ss 403-404). Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given (or, for the car, where the appropriate percentage is not in the deposited text). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Employee case`  @desc Any company car, cheap loan and termination
GIVETH A `Employee position`
`the employee position for` c MEANS
    `Employee position` WITH
        `appropriate percentage for the car`            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the car`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN `the appropriate percentage for` k
        `cash equivalent of the car`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the car`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN `the cash equivalent of my car` k
        `cash equivalent of the loan`                   IS
            CONSIDER c's `the loan`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST l  THEN JUST (`the cash equivalent of my loan` l)
        `earliest lawful termination date`              IS
            CONSIDER c's `the termination`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the earliest lawful termination date for` t)
        `post-employment notice pay`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the termination`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`my post-employment notice pay for` t)
        `taxed as earnings under s 402B`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `the termination`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the part taxed as earnings under s 402B for` t)
        `taxed above the £30,000 threshold`             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the termination`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the part taxed above the threshold for` t)
